  "title": "Jay Leno Decides It’s Time for a New Hobby",
  "summary": "In 1891, there was a huge train accident called the Great Kipton Train Wreck, near Cleveland. One train slammed into another because one of the conductors had a watch that was four minutes off. The railroad investigators hired a Cleveland jeweler, Webb C. Ball, to investigate timekeeping issues on the railroad. Based on his recommendations, […]",
